## Project 1: Claude Feedback Tool (HHHH Feedback Loop)
**AI-powered feedback-to-code platform for non-developers** | Solo project | ~29.6k lines of TypeScript

**One-line summary:**
Local AI development workflow tool jisme koi non-technical user plain language mein change request deta hai, aur Claude us request ko analysis, plan, approval, implementation, validation aur pull request tak governed tareeke se le jaata hai.

**Tech stack:**
- **AI:** Claude Agent SDK (`@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`), agentic multi-phase workflow, prompt engineering, read-only vs write permission enforcement
- **Backend:** Node.js, Express 5, TypeScript, Zod (schema validation), YAML, `diff`
- **Frontend:** React 19, Vite 6, TypeScript, MSAL (`@azure/msal-browser`, Microsoft auth)
- **Tooling:** Git/GitHub PR automation, dev-server orchestration, Node test runner (13 test files)

**Resume bullets:**
- Designed and built an end-to-end AI feedback-to-code workflow (Feedback → Analysis → Clarification → Impact Plan → Approval → Implementation → Validation → Review → PR) on the Claude Agent SDK, so non-developers can ship changes without knowing code or git.
- Implemented host-enforced safety: analysis and planning phases are read-only, and writes are allowed only after the exact plan is approved. A scope fence restricts Claude to the files the plan declares, and a command guard blocks unsafe shell operations.
- Built a "grill" step where the AI asks clarifying questions before coding. It then generates an impact analysis that marks unverifiable items as "unknown" rather than "safe".
- Added a governance layer: change classes, CR-numbered change specs, policy-pack checks, decision log, role tiers (commenter / requester / approver), audit trail and approval locking.
- Automated validation: the tool runs the project's own build, type-check, tests and lint, and reports real exit codes. It also compares failures against the last commit to show whether the change caused them.
- Automated Git/GitHub: one branch per change (`cr/<year>-<nnnn>`), descriptive commits, PR creation, unsaved-work detection, and one-click undo/rollback.
- Built a Simple mode (plain language, screenshot attachments, multilingual answers, try-it-before-approve) alongside an Expert mode with full diffs and logs.
- Added project auto-discovery (SPFx, Vite, npm scripts), dev-server launch, and a "setup request" flow (clone repo, configure `.env`, install, run).
- Added secrets redaction, per-project locking, token and usage tracking, and test fakes (fake agent, fake GitHub) for deterministic testing.

